        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a1086a60-c0f5-5108-bfda-1baa60c84696",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Tron; The Million Dollar Duck; Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure\n- People: Steven Lisberger; Bonnie MacBird; Jeff Bridges; Dan Shor\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: Ram; Billy the Kid\n- Concepts: mainframe computer; software world\n\nFacts:\n- The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Tron is a 1982 American science fiction action-adventure film written and directed by Steven Lisberger and based on a story by Steven Lisberger and Bonnie MacBird.\n- Tron was produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Jeff Bridges stars in Tron as a computer programmer who is transported into the software world of a mainframe computer and interacts with programs while trying to escape.\n- Dan Shor is recognized for playing Ram in Tron in 1982.\n- Dan Shor is also recognized for playing Billy the Kid in Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure in 1989.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cd3e0398-466c-505c-932b-2994a8e91a11",
        "text": "Page: Tron. Sentence: Tron is a 1982 American science fiction action-adventure film written and directed by Steven Lisberger, based on a story by Lisberger and Bonnie MacBird and produced by Walt Disney Productions.\nPage: Tron. Sentence: The film stars Jeff Bridges as a computer programmer who is transported inside the software world of a mainframe computer where he interacts with programs in his attempt to escape.\nPage: The Million Dollar Duck. Sentence: The Million Dollar Duck (also titled as The $1,000,000 Duck) is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs scenario.\nPage: Dan Shor. Sentence: His most recognized roles include Ram in \"Tron\" (1982) and Billy the Kid in \"Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure\" (1989).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
